<title>USA: U.S. grain prices at Gulf export points - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. grain prices at Gulf export points - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gulf export bids for grain delivered to gulf export elevators, barge to Louisiana gulf, rail to Texas gulf, prompt or 30 day shipment, dollar per bushel, except sorghum per cwt. Change in Cents. -- USDA</p>
<p>			  Basis     Bids	     Change</p>
<p>No 1 hrw wheat	  +58  4.74		up 9</p>
<p>No 2 srw wheat     +26+28  4.0475-4.0675   up 3.75</p>
<p>No 2 yellow corn   +30+31  2.9750-2.9850   up 5-3</p>
<p>No 2 sorghum rail	-2  4.74		up 5</p>
<p>		barge  +11+12  4.97-4.99	 up 7-5</p>
<p>No 1 soybeans	+35+37  7.2000-7.2200   dn .75-up .25</p>
<p>Cash bids reflect the difference between the basis and the futures settlement. (Kansas City Dec HRWW; Chicago Dec SRWW; Chicago Dec Corn; Chicago Dec Corn Sorghum and Chicago Jan Soybeans.)</p>
<p>(Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720)</p>
